66:        <details>
85:      <section class="chapter-section" id="orientation">
86:        <span class="section-number">00</span>
87:        <h2 class="section-title">Begin with the failure, not the slogan</h2>
88:        <p class="section-lead">You ask an AI to write a function. It gives you plausible code. You paste it into the repository, discover that it does not fit, repair two imports, run the tests, fix a test, create a branch, make the commit, and explain the result in Slack. The AI helped with one narrow slice. You still carried the workflow.</p>
94:        <aside class="callout callout--tactic">
95:          <p class="callout__label">The chapter’s one-sentence thesis</p>
99:        <h3>What you are training</h3>
100:        <ul class="learning-objectives">
107:        <h3>How to use this chapter</h3>
110:        <div class="callout callout--warning">
111:          <p class="callout__label">Prime directive for every exercise</p>
116:      <section class="chapter-section idea-cycle" id="idea-role">
117:        <span class="section-number">01</span>
118:        <h2 class="section-title">A new role: the Agentic Engineer</h2>
119:        <p class="section-lead">The title matters only if the work changes. “Agentic Engineer” is not a badge for someone who uses AI often; it names an engineer who builds systems able to take engineering actions.</p>
121:        <div class="move move--hook">
122:          <p class="move-label">1 · Hook — concrete failure</p>
123:          <h3>The prompt expert who is still the workflow engine</h3>
128:        <div class="move move--picture">
129:          <p class="move-label">2 · Picture — the two-phase map</p>
130:          <h3>Move the boundary of delegation</h3>
131:          <div class="comparison" aria-label="AI coding and agentic coding roles compared">
132:            <article class="comparison__card">
133:              <div class="comparison__head"><h3>Phase 1 · AI coding</h3><p>The agent produces code; the human carries the workflow.</p></div>
134:              <div class="comparison__body">
135:                <div class="workflow workflow--stacked">
136:                  <div class="workflow__step"><strong>Human</strong><code>context → prompt</code></div>
137:                  <div class="workflow__step"><strong>Agent</strong><code>generate code</code></div>
138:                  <div class="workflow__step"><strong>Human</strong><code>write → run → fix → commit → report</code></div>
142:            <article class="comparison__card comparison__card--agentic">
143:              <div class="comparison__head"><h3>Phase 2 · Agentic coding</h3><p>The human specifies and reviews; the agent carries the workflow.</p></div>
144:              <div class="comparison__body">
145:                <div class="workflow workflow--stacked">
146:                  <div class="workflow__step"><strong>Human</strong><code>goal + constraints + checks</code></div>
147:                  <div class="workflow__step"><strong>Agent</strong><code>branch → write → run → commit → report</code></div>
148:                  <div class="workflow__step"><strong>Human</strong><code>review outcome + improve loop</code></div>
156:        <div class="move move--story">
157:          <p class="move-label">3 · Story of one move — Dan’s demo</p>
158:          <h3>A 2023 bet becomes a visible phase change</h3>
160:          <figure class="frame-card">
162:            <figcaption><span class="frame-card__t">1:55</span>Dan places AI coding and agentic coding on a two-phase timeline. Keep this scaffold visible: phase two is a superset, not a rejection, of phase one.</figcaption>
167:        <div class="move move--name">
168:          <p class="move-label">4 · Name it — Dan term + plain English</p>
169:          <h3>Phase-two Agentic Engineer</h3>
170:          <aside class="callout callout--term">
171:            <p class="callout__label">Dan’s term</p>
