  ],
  "what_each_does": {
    "README.md": "The system's own teaching doc: how-it-works, quick start (just v / vsql / vpy / vimg), direction matrix, verifier state machine, the review-constraint framing, the CONFIDENCE ladder, the three-layer security model, and known v1 limitations.",
    "justfile": "Every workflow recipe. `v` (generic verifier), `vsql` (SQLite), `vpy` (Python), `vimg` (image) each boot a builder Pi and auto-spawn the matching verifier. Also `clean` (kill stale tmux/sockets/breadcrumbs) and `prime`/`primepi`. Each recipe loads verifiable.ts + cross-agent.ts and passes --verifiable [--verifier-agent <name>].",
    "apps/verifier/verifiable.ts": "BUILDER-side extension. Owns the unix-socket SERVER, spawns the verifier child (via launcher), forwards lifecycle ticks (before_agent_start→start, agent_end→stop, crashes→error), captures per-turn session-file line offsets + the original user prompt, receives prompt/report envelopes, injects corrections via pi.sendUserMessage(deliverAs:'followUp'), and enforces max_loops escalation. Registers the /verify command.",
    "apps/verifier/verifier.ts": "VERIFIER-side extension (runs in the --child Pi). Replaces the editor with a locked, color-coded status bar; connects to the parent socket; on each stop event templates verify_on_stop.md and injects it; exposes the verifier_prompt tool (the only outbound channel); enforces the script-only bash policy via a tool_call hook; parses the '## Report' block (STATUS + CONFIDENCE + sections) on its own agent_end and ships a report envelope back.",
    "apps/verifier/verifiable-footer.ts": "BuilderInputEditor — embeds verifier-connection status, model id, and context-usage % into the builder input box's borders (top-right: verifier connected/spawning/disconnected; bottom-left: model; bottom-right: ctx %).",
    "apps/verifier/cross-agent.ts": "Loads commands/skills/agents from .claude/ .gemini/ .codex/ (project + global) into the BUILDER only — so the builder can invoke /prime, the gpt-image-2 skill, etc. Explicitly NOT loaded into the verifier (read-only by architecture must not gain arbitrary slash commands).",
    "apps/verifier/_shared/ipc.ts": "The wire protocol: discriminated-union envelope types (hello/hello_ack/prompt/prompt_ack/report/event/ping/pong/bye), JSONL framing that splits on \\n ONLY (never Node readline — it would split on U+2028/U+2029 inside JSON strings), and assertDirection() enforcing the asymmetric direction matrix.",
    "apps/verifier/_shared/launcher.ts": "$TMUX-aware spawn. In-tmux → sibling window; native terminal → detached tmux session + a new OS window (per-emulator dispatch: Ghostty/iTerm/Terminal.app/WezTerm/gnome-terminal/konsole/kitty/alacritty/xterm, else osascript Terminal.app). Renders the persona system prompt, writes a wrapper script (sidesteps macOS ARG_MAX), passes --tools (persona allowlist + verifier_prompt) and --model (persona model).",
    "apps/verifier/_shared/socket-path.ts": "Resolves the socket to /tmp/pi-verifier/<sid>.sock (short path to stay under macOS's 104-byte sun_path limit), ensures the dir is mode 0700 (the authentication), and writes/reads the .pi/state/verifier-<sid>.sock.ref breadcrumb.",
    "apps/verifier/_shared/frontmatter.ts": "Parses + validates verifier persona frontmatter (required: name/description/tools/model/domain; optional: bash_policy{mode,allowed_script,runner}, max_loops, verification_focus) and does the dumb <UPPER_SNAKE> template substitution for persona/prompt bodies.",
    "apps/verifier/_shared/env.ts": "loadDotEnv — both agents load .env from cwd on session_start; existing process.env wins, .env fills gaps (defensive because tmux env inheritance is unreliable).",
    ".pi/verifier/agents/verifier.md": "GENERIC persona (model openai/gpt-5.5, no bash_policy). Decomposes any request into atomic claims and verifies with read/grep/find/ls/bash (read-only by prompt only). NOT a non-functional stub — it is a full working persona on disk (the README's 'v1 limitations' text is out of date here).",
    ".pi/verifier/agents/verify_sqlite.md": "SQLite persona. bash_policy script-only → verify_sqlite.py; verification_focus: schemas/FKs/indexes/integrity/migrations. On disk model=openai/gpt-5.5; the video showed model=z-ai/glm-5.1.",
    ".pi/verifier/agents/verify_image.md": "Image persona. Vision-capable, no bash_policy (vision is the oracle). Encodes the readability contract: MAX_TEXT_ELEMENTS=10 distinct text blocks; illegible/overloaded text is a readability FAIL with a concrete fix. Has a relevance gate (no image work → no-op PERFECT).",
    ".pi/verifier/agents/verify_python.md": "Python persona. bash_policy script-only → verify_python.py. Runs uvx ty / uvx ruff check / ruff format --check / pytest / coverage; tests are conditional on the project's existing test posture; always uv/uvx, never bare python/pip. Relevance gate for non-Python turns.",
    ".pi/verifier/scripts/verify_sqlite.py": "The ONLY bash command the SQLite verifier may run. Opens the DB mode=ro&immutable=1, routes dot-commands through sqlite3 -readonly, allows SELECT/WITH/EXPLAIN, enforces a PRAGMA allowlist (introspective only). Every refusal is structured JSON {error,received,reason,allowed,hint} — 'the error message is the documentation.'",
    ".pi/verifier/scripts/verify_python.py": "The Python verifier's single allowed script. Subcommands type/lint/format/test/coverage shell out to check-only Astral tools + pytest and return JSON {command,exit_code,stdout,stderr}.",
    ".pi/verifier/prompts/verify_on_stop.md": "The per-cycle user prompt template, rendered on every builder stop event with TURN_INDEX, TIMESTAMP, the [start..end] line slice, and the ORIGINAL user prompt. Tells the verifier to read only the slice, verify each claim, prompt back on failure, and end on exactly one ## Report block. Same template across all domains.",
    ".pi/verifier/prompts/builder_error.md": "Rendered when the builder emits an error event — surfaces the detail; no verification action (verifier stays idle until the next stop).",
    ".claude/skills/gpt-image-2/SKILL.md": "The image-authoring skill the BUILDER invokes in the vimg demo. Wraps OpenAI gpt-image-2 (generate + edit/inpaint/compose). Uses OPENAI_API_KEY; --quality is the effective effort dial; documents sizes/formats/pricing. Also used to author the repo's own arch diagrams.",
    ".claude/commands/prime.md": "The /prime context primer — walks an agent through the README, the runtime TypeScript, the SQLite domain contract, and the justfile in one shot.",
    ".claude/commands/install.md": "The /install readiness check — verifies CLIs (node/pi/tmux/uv/python3/sqlite3/just), npm install, persona/script validity, provider key presence, and npx tsc --noEmit. Never starts a Pi session.",
    "images/arch-loop.svg": "The animated two-agent observer architecture embedded at the top of the README (engineer → builder → session.jsonl → verifier → correction back to builder).",
    "images/07-two-camps.svg": "The 'two camps' diagram — Camp A (stuck in prompt→babysit→re-prompt) vs Camp B (builder + verifier coordinated: build·verify·feedback·repeat).",
    "images/verifier.png": "The two-agent runtime screenshot (builder Pi left, verifier Pi right, communicating over a unix socket)."
  },
  "generated_not_committed": {
    "arch.jpg / arch copy.jpg": "The architecture diagram the builder generates via the gpt-image-2 skill in the vimg demo (and the backup Dan clones before it's overwritten). Runtime artifacts, not part of the shipped source.",
    "tmp/mock_shop.db / tmp/mock_shop_backup.db": "The fixture SQLite databases used in the vsql demo (users/products/orders[/discounts]). Created at demo time.",
    "/tmp/pi-verifier/<sid>.sock": "The unix domain socket the builder binds (dir chmod 0700). Unlinked on shutdown.",
    ".pi/state/verifier-<sid>.sock.ref": "Breadcrumb pointing at the socket so `ls .pi/state/` shows running verifier sessions and the child resolves the socket by session id alone.",
    "~/.pi/agent/sessions/<sid>.jsonl": "The builder's session transcript on disk. The verifier reads only the [start..end] slice for the turn being verified."
  }
}
